---
import LegalPage from '../components/legal/LegalPage.astro';

import { formatLegalDate } from '../data/legal';
import { websitePrivacyUpdated } from '../data/website-privacy';

const lastUpdated = formatLegalDate(websitePrivacyUpdated);
---

<LegalPage
  metaTitle="Website Privacy Policy — HebrewEdu"
  description="How the HebrewEdu website (hebrewedu.com) uses Google Analytics, when consent is asked for, and how to change your choice."
  title="Website Privacy Policy"
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
>
    <section>
      <h2>Scope</h2>
      <p>This page covers only the HebrewEdu website at hebrewedu.com. For the HebrewEdu mobile apps, see the <a href="/privacy/">app Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
      <p>The website uses Google Analytics 4 (GA4), provided by Google, to understand how the site is used — for example, which pages are visited and which in-app links are followed.</p>
      <p>If you are in the European Economic Area, the UK or Switzerland, Google Analytics only runs after you accept it in the consent notice shown when you first visit. If you decline, it is never loaded, and no analytics cookies are set. Outside those regions, Google Analytics runs by default, consistent with applicable law, and you can still opt out at any time (see "Your choice" below).</p>
      <p>When it runs, Google Analytics may process technical and usage data such as pages viewed, browser and device information, approximate location derived from your IP address, and interactions with the website (for example clicks on links to our app's store pages or lesson/practice activity). It may set cookies or similar identifiers in your browser.</p>
      <p>Advertising features are switched off: the website does not enable Google signals or ad personalization, and ad-related consent signals (<code>ad_storage</code>, <code>ad_user_data</code>, <code>ad_personalization</code>) are always denied. We do not intentionally send your name, email address, or any text you type to Google Analytics.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your choice</h2>
      <p>You can change your analytics choice at any time using the "Privacy choices" link at the bottom of every page — it reopens the consent notice, wherever you are. Your choice is stored in your browser's local storage on your device, not on our servers. If you withdraw consent, analytics stops and we try to remove Google Analytics cookies (<code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code>); you can also clear them yourself in your browser settings.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>Google Analytics data is retained in our GA4 property for up to 14 months, after which it is automatically deleted, per Google's standard GA4 retention settings.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Google's processing</h2>
      <p>Google processes data according to its own policies: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use its services</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this page: <a href="mailto:vicsothemes@gmail.com">vicsothemes@gmail.com</a></p>
    </section>
</LegalPage>
